diff --git a/docs/privacy-audit.md b/docs/privacy-audit.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..31fe88d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/privacy-audit.md
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+# Privacy audit
+
+Scope: sign-in and sign-up forms, the shared document layout, document headers, and related user notices.
+
+## Changes
+
+- Kept the existing API contract at username and password only; no email, name, consent record, or profile data added. Suggested pseudonyms and unique passwords.
+- Added a shared notice before submission identifying the external authentication service, the purpose of collection, and connection metadata disclosure. Linked directly to account privacy information.
+- Authentication requests use HTTPS POST, omit cookies, suppress referrers, bypass the browser cache, and reject redirects so credentials are not forwarded to another destination. Responses are not parsed or echoed; errors are generic and passwords are cleared after success or failure. No credential or token storage or logging was added.
+- Added password-manager autocomplete, stable field names, accessible help/status messages, password visibility controls, and native validation matching the existing sign-up password instructions. Controls stay disabled until hydration, avoiding accidental native submissions before JavaScript is ready or when it is unavailable.
+- Removed automatic analytics, the dormant ad script reference, ad-slot registration, Google Fonts stylesheet, and preconnections from the layout. The existing serif fallback supplies typography without remote font requests.
+- Removed eager initialization of empty reading-list sessions on every request. The existing reading-list endpoints already default to an empty list and create a session when a bookmark is written, avoiding unnecessary visitor cookies.
+- Added UTF-8 and no-referrer metadata, plus response headers for no-referrer, nosniff, and disabling camera, microphone, and geolocation. Authentication documents also receive no-store and noindex/nofollow headers. The middleware covers on-demand Astro routes; static assets are managed by the deployment host.
+- Replaced the generic privacy policy with implementation-specific information and replaced the nonfunctional privacy-preferences link with a link to the tracking explanation.
+
+## Remaining operator responsibilities
+
+The external authentication service is not implemented in this repository. Its retention period, password hashing, account deletion, access controls, rate limits, and response-cache policy cannot be established here. The frontend's no-store request option does not establish server-side retention. A verified privacy contact and operational deletion/access process are still needed before real accounts are invited.
+
+The existing login flow reports authentication success without establishing a local authenticated session; this change preserves that behavior and does not persist returned tokens. Cross-origin requests still expose the browser's Origin header and connection metadata to the authentication service.
+
+Hosting logs, externally hosted article media, article-specific demonstration scripts/cookies, and reading-list sessions remain separate data flows. The notice discloses them; it does not claim the whole site is free of cookies or third-party requests. The article demonstrations and origin-check configuration were outside this focused change.
+
+## Validation scope
+
+Static source review and production build only. Production build passed, with existing Vite plugin deprecation and dynamic-route prerender warnings. `git diff --check` passed. No browser verification, development/preview server, server-entrypoint import, or live authentication request was performed.
+
+## References
+
+- [Astro middleware](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/middleware/)
+- [MDN referrer policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Referrer-Policy)
