+    <h2 id="accounts">Accounts and authentication</h2>
+    <p>Sign-up and sign-in ask only for a username and password. No name, email address, phone number, or marketing preferences are requested. Choose a nickname and a unique password, and do not enter sensitive personal information.</p>
+    <p>Submitting either form sends only those two fields over HTTPS to the times_cdn authentication service at <code>us-central1-web-devrel-apps.cloudfunctions.net</code>, using its <code>/times_cdn/api/register</code> or <code>/times_cdn/api/login</code> endpoint. The service receives your IP address and other connection information as part of the request. Requests omit cookies and referrer information and do not follow redirects.</p>
+    <p>The forms do not log credentials or save credentials or returned tokens in browser storage. The password field is cleared after every completed request. Your browser or password manager may offer to save credentials under your own settings.</p>
+    <p>The external authentication service is outside this repository. Its password storage, retention period, access controls, and account deletion process have not been verified here. This demo has no account deletion interface. Do not use it with credentials or personal details you use for other services.</p>
+
+    <h2 id="privacy-preferences">Analytics, advertising, and fonts</h2>
+    <p>The shared page layout does not load third-party analytics, advertising scripts, or remote fonts. There is no optional tracking enabled by this layout and no tracking consent stored by it.</p>
+
+    <h2>Other requests and storage</h2>
+    <p>The hosting service receives the requests needed to deliver pages and assets, including your IP address. Hosting log contents and retention are controlled by the deployment operator and have not been verified in this repository.</p>
+    <p>Some articles contain externally hosted images or links. Loading external images shares connection information with their hosts; following a link takes you to another service. The site uses a no-referrer policy to avoid sending the current page address with those requests.</p>
+    <p>The reading-list feature uses server-side session storage and may require a session cookie. Some demonstration articles also set cookies or make requests for their examples. You can remove site cookies and stored site data through your browser settings; doing so may reset your reading list.</p>
+
+    <h2>Questions and requests</h2>
+    <p>Consult the <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}legal/imprint`}>Imprint</a> for publisher information. This demo does not provide a verified privacy contact or a self-service data access or deletion process. Those details and the external service's retention practices need to be established by the operator before real accounts are invited.</p>
